DIAG: ath12k: mark each step of ath12k_core_start

Temporary, not for upstream.

All 25 datapath rings now complete, and the panic lands about 49 ms after
the last one -- inside ath12k_core_start(), which runs thirteen steps in
sequence. The first of them, ath12k_hif_start(), enables the copy engine
interrupts and posts RX buffers, so it is the first point at which the
firmware writes into memory the host allocated.

Print a mark before each step so the log says which one is running when
procd dies.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
